I would really love to hear the other implementer's opinion on this.

I still think that it would come as a surprise if layers didn't observed global states. If they didn't, the following would code would blend the first and third `fillRect`, but not the layer in between. Web pages would need to repeat the alpha in the `beginLayer` call.
```
ctx.globalAlpha(0.5);
ctx.fillRect(0, 0, 10, 10);
ctx.beginLayer();
ctx.fillRect(10, 0, 10, 10);
ctx.endLayer();
ctx.fillRect(20, 0, 10, 10);
```

